g:** a medication card inside a group shows \"Oral · 5 mg\" instead of \"Capsule · 5 mg\". The Medicines list shows the correct \"Capsule · 5 mg\" for the same medicine. The same wrong \"Oral\" caption also appears in the Active groups row on the medicine detail screen. This is the shared caption helper that changed in this build.\n\n**What I checked and found fine:**\n- **Add medicine:** the form options for each category (Estradiol, Antiandrogen, SERM, GnRHa, Custom), plus saving a Custom Capsule and an Estradiol Gel.\n- **Editing medicines:** I changed the gel concentration, and the capsule strength and unit, and the saved values showed correctly.\n- **Body weight editor (Settings):** unit switch kg to lb (70 kg showed 154.3 lb), save, reopen, rotate, and Clear. All behaved correctly.\n- **Settings screen:** layout and toggles looked right.\n\n**What I didn't cover:**\n- I did not save a Patch, Tablet or Injection medicine.\n- I did not try the Sachet or Vial options.\n- I did not test group editing beyond creating one group.\n- Custom only offers Tablet and Capsule as forms, which may be by design.\n\n**One thing I left unreported:** in the Injection form, selecting Ampule labels the field \"Vial strength (mg)\". I couldn't tell whether that wording is intended.\n\nTyping into the Custom medicine name field appended text to what was already there, so the test medicine is saved as \"5estMeTestMeTestMed\". That may be an input-tool quirk rather than an app bug, and I didn't investigate it.\n\nThe test data is still on the device: that medicine, an Estradiol Gel medicine, and \"Group 1\" containing the Custom medicine. The body weight is back to Not set.", "ttft_ms": 1389, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 150682, "uuid": "1015b4bc-2d64-4b23-845b-36987d1c97d8", "ttft_stream_ms": 1017, "time_to_request_ms": 113, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 4, "system_prompt": 14, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 2, "input_attachments": 4, "input_hooks": 2, "convers